[LLM = Large Language Model]
LLM is an AI model trained on huge amounts of text so it can understand and generate human-like language.

How it works :-
User: "What is RAG ?"
       ↓
      LLM
       ↓
Understands the question
       ↓
Generates an answer

Examples of LLMs include: GPT, Claude, Gemini, Llama

[LLM vs RAG]
LLM = The model that generates the answer.
RAG = A system that finds relevant information and gives it to the LLM before it answers.

How it works :-
                 RAG
                  │
User Question → Retriever → Relevant Documents
                                  │
                                  ▼
                              ┌───────┐
                              │  LLM  │
                              └───────┘
                                  │
                                  ▼
                                Answer
